do you need a vacation  i got a great question from my video  producer  christina now if you're liking the  videos that you're seeing christina has  a hand in all of them  put in the beginning intro music effects  all of that's cristina's hard work  and she just came back from a vacation  to engar watt and she wrote in to say  how about a theme for the video is there  a need for vacation to reload your brain  to work better  this is a really interesting topic for  me so i think it's great to go on  vacation i  i equate going on vacation to  learning something new gaining new  experiences because when you  are learning something new  you're able to bring more to your  business you're able to add more value  you're able to make more money as a  result you have new creative ideas  if you're stuck doing the same thing  over and over and over and over and over  and over and over and over and over  again  you get bored it gets boring life gets  boring you stop thinking of creative  ways to make things different  and you can get stuck in a rut where you  you don't know what to do you just know  that your life sucks  you don't know how you got here and you  don't know how to escape  so you need to find ways for you to grow  and try new things and vacationing is a  great way to do it  i love going on vacations i try to do  two long ones  per year and then two shorter ones per  year  and i find that i get tons of new ideas  and new energy  just seeing how business is done in  europe or seeing how entrepreneurs are  kicking in asia what they're up to  gives me ideas on what i can do for my  business  i think it also adds to to your  knowledge level  and to your creativity so  this goes beyond just vacationing it's  just trying out new things i could talk  about  salsa dancing or i could talk about  snowboarding or i could talk about  playing the piano or get a new condo or  cooking or things that i'm  learning and and growing with i can  share those experiences and that makes 